    "pages":  {
                  "4030465":  {
                                  "title":  "Auth Service Troubleshooting Runbook",
                                  "storage":  "\u003ch2 local-id=\"6d4726356b05\"\u003e\u003cac:emoticon ac:name=\"mag\" ac:emoji-shortname=\":mag:\" ac:emoji-id=\"1f50d\" ac:local-id=\"b55eba018cc9\" ac:emoji-fallback=\"🔍\" /\u003e Overview\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"40d7b0af79f9\"\u003eThis runbook covers diagnosis and resolution of authentication service failures affecting user login. The auth service (\u003ccode\u003eauth-service\u003c/code\u003e) runs behind the load balancer \u003ccode\u003eauth-lb-01\u003c/code\u003e and handles all login, token issuance, and session validation requests.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch2 local-id=\"f48f261e5b3c\"\u003e\u003cac:emoticon ac:name=\"warning\" ac:emoji-shortname=\":warning:\" ac:emoji-id=\"atlassian-warning\" ac:local-id=\"d53e495fd311\" ac:emoji-fallback=\":warning:\" /\u003e Symptoms\u003c/h2\u003e\u003ctable data-table-width=\"760\" data-layout=\"default\" ac:local-id=\"a16fbbb75395\" data-table-display-mode=\"default\"\u003e\u003ctbody\u003e\u003ctr ac:local-id=\"ae555c3037c6\"\u003e\u003cth ac:local-id=\"05506cc206bc\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"b0bdfcf066b1\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSymptom\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/th\u003e\u003cth ac:local-id=\"c1d5fdc27a39\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"77cc87b24d98\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDetails\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/th\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr ac:local-id=\"05566bfe4ebb\"\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"468f0df71717\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"2f74de42f35c\"\u003eUsers receive a generic error message on the login page\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"dad6e604a9aa\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"46c25712818c\" /\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr ac:local-id=\"c7732e78ee4c\"\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"bb0ab77f3406\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"038680d2f0ba\"\u003eHTTP 503 responses from the auth endpoint\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"b6ff703ce4cc\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"9ff8bfbaec6e\" /\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr ac:local-id=\"ecfb58712519\"\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"17d3fc8dbd90\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"595f0f0db81c\"\u003eLogin success rate drops below 95% (normal baseline: 99.9%)\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"9fc26b090595\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"74bb7b509d68\" /\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr ac:local-id=\"6fef1ef6721b\"\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"19265d63f6fa\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"b1c198c3a938\"\u003eIncreased error rate visible in Datadog dashboard under \u003ccode\u003eauth-service.error_rate\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"25494288dec3\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"53a21c7c3102\" /\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003c/tbody\u003e\u003c/table\u003e\u003ch2 local-id=\"17549ae84a6c\"\u003e\u003cac:emoticon ac:name=\"cog\" ac:emoji-shortname=\":gear:\" ac:emoji-id=\"2699\" ac:local-id=\"6e930aca5efd\" ac:emoji-fallback=\"âï¸\" /\u003e Step 1 \u0026mdash; Check Service Health\u003c/h2\u003e\u003ctable data-table-width=\"760\" data-layout=\"default\" ac:local-id=\"e8b519c53794\" data-table-display-mode=\"default\"\u003e\u003ctbody\u003e\u003ctr ac:local-id=\"9d242554e620\"\u003e\u003cth ac:local-id=\"9dac173918a3\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"2f4b336c12f8\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eStep\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/th\u003e\u003cth ac:local-id=\"6b1a3514039f\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"c245c04ad4cc\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDetails\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/th\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr ac:local-id=\"eee9d668c1a8\"\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"d44935be8e7e\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"898b1113ca73\"\u003e1. Open the auth service health endpoint\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"fa13b7446b05\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"43e5a1e6ad94\"\u003e\u003ccode\u003ehttps://auth-service.internal/health\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr ac:local-id=\"0b703c2c9878\"\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"ccb708b159cb\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"a9110adb4942\"\u003e2. Expected response\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"4851ce82bc83\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"7aac8c82a568\"\u003e{\u0026quot;status\u0026quot;: \u0026quot;healthy\u0026quot;, \u0026quot;db\u0026quot;: \u0026quot;connected\u0026quot;, \u0026quot;cache\u0026quot;: \u0026quot;connected\u0026quot;}\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr ac:local-id=\"adb33d02ff50\"\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"aa96f7962b0c\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"aa12e24da0ca\"\u003e3. If the response is missing or returns an error, proceed to Step 2.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"e9fb07eade29\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"1b320a31ac0d\" /\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr ac:local-id=\"e223eaee0762\"\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"695cbad4dd80\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"b1e61001962f\"\u003e4. Check the load balancer status at\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"b24df8c9a69a\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"c82d3d429527\"\u003e\u003ccode\u003ehttps://auth-lb-01.internal/status\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003c/tbody\u003e\u003c/table\u003e\u003ch2 local-id=\"86e3d666a510\"\u003e\u003cac:emoticon ac:name=\"blue-star\" ac:emoji-shortname=\":lock:\" ac:emoji-id=\"1f512\" ac:local-id=\"6cb45ad14a4a\" ac:emoji-fallback=\"🔒\" /\u003e Step 2 \u0026mdash; Check SSL Certificate Expiry\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"ee8a9b018a0f\"\u003eSSL certificate expiry is the most common cause of auth service failures.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ctable data-table-width=\"760\" data-layout=\"default\" ac:local-id=\"9a9f3d776763\" data-table-display-mode=\"default\"\u003e\u003ctbody\u003e\u003ctr ac:local-id=\"33f0aea77dad\"\u003e\u003cth ac:local-id=\"513cfdabea39\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"a67abc202b65\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eStep\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/th\u003e\u003cth ac:local-id=\"ee24bf2e6d7d\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"d10a0a280caa\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDetails\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/th\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr ac:local-id=\"c05bc54bfc29\"\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"ba85d59ee4b0\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"9d8c72f0280b\"\u003e1. Run:\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"97a5689d36a2\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"a59ec6f01e85\"\u003e\u003ccode\u003eopenssl s_client -connect auth-lb-01.internal:443 2\u0026gt;/dev/null | openssl x509 -noout -dates\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr ac:local-id=\"8dee5b4e4649\"\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"68eb684621cf\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"ad9447c43f77\"\u003e2. Check the \u003ccode\u003enotAfter\u003c/code\u003e date. If the certificate has expired or expires within 7 days, renew it immediately.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"2777c7024889\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"30ede82ecd5a\" /\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr ac:local-id=\"a1a4494de373\"\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"b348a7429188\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"a093220e9996\"\u003e3. To renew using Let\u0027s Encrypt:\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"7d2c16435a1b\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"042cb681d31c\"\u003e\u003ccode\u003esudo certbot renew --force-renewal --nginx\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr ac:local-id=\"5b68f986dfbf\"\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"4c734381bd15\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"495c3f77c4e2\"\u003e4. Reload nginx after renewal:\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"b9479c1a69e8\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"537a452bdb7c\"\u003e\u003ccode\u003esudo systemctl reload nginx\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr ac:local-id=\"31ca42d82718\"\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"8a3cebfe8c9e\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"c914f742f240\"\u003e5. Verify: re-run the openssl command and confirm the new expiry date.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"86a4463dfff5\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"155e66b2a941\" /\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr ac:local-id=\"56223b13aded\"\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"7e52ca6aafcb\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"dd4e54914776\"\u003e6. Monitor login success rate for 5 minutes after the fix.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"a07d1344a03a\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"159dd0d657f6\" /\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003c/tbody\u003e\u003c/table\u003e\u003ch2 local-id=\"4c043e50cbe0\"\u003e\u003cac:emoticon ac:name=\"blue-star\" ac:emoji-shortname=\":file_cabinet:\" ac:local-id=\"b01bf5620f86\" ac:emoji-fallback=\"📁\" /\u003e Step 3 \u0026mdash; Check Auth Service Logs\u003c/h2\u003e\u003ctable data-table-width=\"760\" data-layout=\"default\" ac:local-id=\"cd717c7d2754\" data-table-display-mode=\"default\"\u003e\u003ctbody\u003e\u003ctr ac:local-id=\"76c5461b5f20\"\u003e\u003cth ac:local-id=\"10b0aad61500\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"2a3535361133\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eStep\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/th\u003e\u003cth ac:local-id=\"15a180a20248\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"022d20200e4b\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDetails\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/th\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr ac:local-id=\"2d6225f538ba\"\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"01155434c971\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"a8118bbed0f0\"\u003e1. SSH to \u003ccode\u003eauth-service-01.internal\u003c/code\u003e or \u003ccode\u003eauth-service-02.internal\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"a214c00de0a2\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"39b51c1dd139\" /\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr ac:local-id=\"cda854f68ad8\"\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"335f23cb6b2e\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"7cec13ee509c\"\u003e2. Tail logs:\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"4b8bc16a2d05\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"d9e632d12eba\"\u003e\u003ccode\u003esudo journalctl -u auth-service -f --since \u0026quot;1 hour ago\u0026quot;\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr ac:local-id=\"c52d2baaf9bb\"\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"9bed7b6fe9d1\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"0cf3cb2d7430\"\u003e3. Look for:\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"5ee50ff7f344\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"dbf15b683cab\"\u003e\u003ccode\u003econnection refused\u003c/code\u003e, \u003ccode\u003ecertificate verify failed\u003c/code\u003e, \u003ccode\u003eupstream timeout\u003c/code\u003e, \u003ccode\u003edatabase connection failed\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr ac:local-id=\"c5de033a772b\"\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"c3f19fbf3d9b\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"a2de013bb686\"\u003e4. If database errors appear, follow the Database Connection Pool runbook.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"2e59e50c20bf\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"03d990e29119\" /\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003c/tbody\u003e\u003c/table\u003e\u003ch2 local-id=\"904cfe652d32\"\u003e\u003cac:emoticon ac:name=\"blue-star\" ac:emoji-shortname=\":recycle:\" ac:local-id=\"91efe06834ce\" ac:emoji-fallback=\"🔁\" /\u003e Step 4 \u0026mdash; Restart the Auth Service\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"2153c22dbe6b\"\u003eIf no root cause is found and the service is unresponsive:\u003c/p\u003e\u003ctable data-table-width=\"760\" data-layout=\"default\" ac:local-id=\"a7d71a6315d3\" data-table-display-mode=\"default\"\u003e\u003ctbody\u003e\u003ctr ac:local-id=\"892227707064\"\u003e\u003cth ac:local-id=\"674713da95dd\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"a2b09078bd41\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eStep\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/th\u003e\u003cth ac:local-id=\"12a3c6d14eac\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"a164f65f9f75\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDetails\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/th\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr ac:local-id=\"669eed44b3ef\"\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"527d4304448c\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"fbd3bc74e78d\"\u003e1. Restart on primary node:\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"698cf5842685\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"8a8145fa7221\"\u003e\u003ccode\u003esudo systemctl restart auth-service\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr ac:local-id=\"e332aad4005d\"\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"57cc386b6df9\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"0886355704d1\"\u003e2. Wait 30 seconds and check health endpoint.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"d7c6a067f736\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"b48a5f4a7149\" /\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr ac:local-id=\"c4c05f3a8522\"\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"f6f91f823626\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"69fc7b6e7f83\"\u003e3. If unhealthy, restart on secondary: SSH to \u003ccode\u003eauth-service-02.internal\u003c/code\u003e and repeat.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"5efbf3610b7e\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"8282022d0fdf\" /\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr ac:local-id=\"d43c7e3124e2\"\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"f1809045039e\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"18784f22ccd5\"\u003e4. Do not restart both nodes simultaneously.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"df4ff0ce6f87\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"6a7bd7220527\" /\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003c/tbody\u003e\u003c/table\u003e\u003ch2 local-id=\"f54f0d9cead4\"\u003e\u003cac:emoticon ac:name=\"blue-star\" ac:emoji-shortname=\":rotating_light:\" ac:emoji-id=\"1f6a8\" ac:local-id=\"60849d2757cb\" ac:emoji-fallback=\"🚨\" /\u003e Step 5 \u0026mdash; Escalation\u003c/h2\u003e\u003ctable data-table-width=\"760\" data-layout=\"default\" ac:local-id=\"95a715b0d4bc\" data-table-display-mode=\"default\"\u003e\u003ctbody\u003e\u003ctr ac:local-id=\"6242fe71d5a5\"\u003e\u003cth ac:local-id=\"96db1b30412d\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"bb38db5194ac\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eCondition\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/th\u003e\u003cth ac:local-id=\"bc18b6b11423\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"28a1c798d6a8\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eAction\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/th\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr ac:local-id=\"9ef68ae5b415\"\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"535d32000d30\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"1bd62526cdce\"\u003eIf the issue is not resolved within 20 minutes:\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"e5e7049b3aea\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"26614b81fc91\"\u003ePage the on-call auth engineer via PagerDuty: escalation policy \u003ccode\u003eAUTH-ONCALL\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr ac:local-id=\"9614a5c20c5a\"\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"3bcd124f7f52\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"ede7c1fd76a2\"\u003e- Notify \u003ccode\u003e#incidents\u003c/code\u003e Slack channel with current status\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"f53d7271c6c0\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"230b9b1c4e6e\" /\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr ac:local-id=\"a2afa0c124df\"\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"53a7e00d64d7\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"2af4bdd358f1\"\u003e- Open a P1 incident ticket if not already created\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"59af41df546c\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"0e3963f7664a\" /\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003c/tbody\u003e\u003c/table\u003e\u003ch2 local-id=\"8132e7e00384\"\u003e\u003cac:emoticon ac:name=\"chart_with_upwards_trend\" ac:emoji-shortname=\":chart_with_upwards_trend:\" ac:emoji-id=\"1f4c8\" ac:local-id=\"7d0185940fe4\" ac:emoji-fallback=\"📈\" /\u003e Monitoring\u003c/h2\u003e\u003ctable data-table-width=\"760\" data-layout=\"default\" ac:local-id=\"37ed4d595b05\" data-table-display-mode=\"default\"\u003e\u003ctbody\u003e\u003ctr ac:local-id=\"21aa3d155f7c\"\u003e\u003cth ac:local-id=\"9df55f5d0269\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"56e99f49ea2d\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eItem\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/th\u003e\u003cth ac:local-id=\"b8a584285c05\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"6fac0150fb0c\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDetails\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/th\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr ac:local-id=\"1246c2280da1\"\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"b332bf752151\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"fd2539d27ac5\"\u003eDatadog dashboard\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"c108d33b6129\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"498ec77e6b0c\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://app.datadoghq.com/dashboard/auth-service\"\u003eAuth Service Overview\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr ac:local-id=\"0819de644013\"\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"ddad96b712fb\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"fb3b85e8657a\"\u003eAlert threshold\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"38d3a3248143\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"f996e284109a\"\u003elogin success rate below 98% for 5 consecutive minutes triggers PagerDuty\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr ac:local-id=\"e5795eea6d66\"\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"01783a31a888\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"cb54fe97eb8a\"\u003eCertificate expiry alert\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"c7aa9d68a28e\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"f9bc800ecadd\"\u003efires 30 days before expiry (monitor: \u003ccode\u003essl-cert-expiry-auth\u003c/code\u003e)\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003c/tbody\u003e\u003c/table\u003e\u003ch2 local-id=\"0a111d743022\"\u003e\u003cac:emoticon ac:name=\"blue-star\" ac:emoji-shortname=\":information_source:\" ac:emoji-id=\"2139\" ac:local-id=\"15b8e516cc32\" ac:emoji-fallback=\"â¹ï¸\" /\u003e Known Issues\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cac:structured-macro ac:name=\"info\" ac:schema-version=\"1\" ac:local-id=\"56f717960e87\" ac:macro-id=\"9789cd6d-aed1-415b-b578-ef8111b95f44\"\u003e\u003cac:parameter ac:name=\"containerLevel\"\u003epanel_c1\u003c/ac:parameter\u003e\u003cac:rich-text-body\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"54738860721f\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eLet\u0027s Encrypt rate limit\u003c/strong\u003e: If certificate renewal fails with a rate limit error, use the staging endpoint for testing and wait 1 hour before retrying production renewal.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/ac:rich-text-body\u003e\u003c/ac:structured-macro\u003e\u003cac:structured-macro ac:name=\"info\" ac:schema-version=\"1\" ac:local-id=\"0b971179d595\" ac:macro-id=\"d47553f7-4d28-4c30-8d60-3e7ae4b1bb44\"\u003e\u003cac:parameter ac:name=\"containerLevel\"\u003epanel_c1\u003c/ac:parameter\u003e\u003cac:rich-text-body\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"b8e98f1432b0\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eCache warmup\u003c/strong\u003e: After a restart, the auth service takes approximately 2 minutes to warm its token cache. Elevated latency during this period is expected.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/ac:rich-text-body\u003e\u003c/ac:structured-macro\u003e"
                              },
                  "4161537":  {
                                  "title":  "Database Connection Pool Troubleshooting",
                                  "storage":  "\u003ch2 local-id=\"9d3b9d1b9fe2\"\u003e\u003cac:emoticon ac:name=\"clipboard\" ac:emoji-shortname=\":clipboard:\" ac:emoji-id=\"1f4cb\" ac:local-id=\"ab4aae020fad\" ac:emoji-fallback=\"📋\" /\u003e Overview\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cac:structured-macro ac:name=\"info\" ac:schema-version=\"1\" ac:local-id=\"bcea9159ba34\" ac:macro-id=\"54f62525-07f2-444e-a977-2bc60d534ed3\"\u003e\u003cac:parameter ac:name=\"containerLevel\"\u003epanel_c1\u003c/ac:parameter\u003e\u003cac:rich-text-body\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"2797d6f2a684\"\u003eThis runbook covers diagnosis and resolution of database connection pool exhaustion on the primary PostgreSQL cluster (`db-primary`). Connection pool exhaustion causes applications to fail with \u0026quot;too many connections\u0026quot; or \u0026quot;connection refused\u0026quot; errors, resulting in slow or failed page loads across all dependent services.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/ac:rich-text-body\u003e\u003c/ac:structured-macro\u003e\u003ch2 local-id=\"21dd3d2a4b66\"\u003e\u003cac:emoticon ac:name=\"warning\" ac:emoji-shortname=\":warning:\" ac:emoji-id=\"atlassian-warning\" ac:local-id=\"152e4f68a864\" ac:emoji-fallback=\":warning:\" /\u003e Symptoms\u003c/h2\u003e\u003ctable data-table-width=\"760\" data-layout=\"default\" ac:local-id=\"1ac6bb2c6ff1\" data-table-display-mode=\"default\"\u003e\u003ctbody\u003e\u003ctr ac:local-id=\"3aca20c6aa40\"\u003e\u003cth ac:local-id=\"97f53b50d075\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"7334d8369389\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSymptom\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/th\u003e\u003cth ac:local-id=\"4c2e8df9931f\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"b2358b9b1fc9\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDetails\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/th\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr ac:local-id=\"c1fa4448826f\"\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"3bae5140c9ce\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"9ba6b3af1407\"\u003eApplications returning 500 errors\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"c09c98d77474\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"e410ee82649d\"\u003eApplications returning 500 errors with message \u0026quot;too many connections\u0026quot;\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr ac:local-id=\"4884c4acce99\"\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"640a50989da1\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"e4322bebe68e\"\u003ePostgreSQL log entries\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"0743606d1cb7\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"b6b4b3270545\"\u003e`FATAL: remaining connection slots are reserved for non-replication superuser connections`\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr ac:local-id=\"366bc249342c\"\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"f253b380446d\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"16d996e7fcab\"\u003eSlow queue loading in JSM\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"9b959f8b62c3\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"16ca59fdda6c\"\u003eQueries taking more than 5 seconds\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr ac:local-id=\"a4a8baee07a7\"\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"79cb5dda23c8\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"862d2bf8abb3\"\u003eDashboard showing connection count\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"4a861e8fe13b\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"afc43e1b1949\"\u003eConnection count near or at `max_connections` (default: 200)\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003c/tbody\u003e\u003c/table\u003e\u003ch2 local-id=\"379878d4c1da\"\u003e\u003cac:emoticon ac:name=\"mag\" ac:emoji-shortname=\":mag:\" ac:emoji-id=\"1f50d\" ac:local-id=\"4c4a584c4d51\" ac:emoji-fallback=\"🔍\" /\u003e Step 1 \u0026mdash; Check Current Connection Count\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cac:structured-macro ac:name=\"code\" ac:schema-version=\"1\" ac:local-id=\"0f7736fe1af5\" ac:macro-id=\"5ef4a939-166e-4d8e-b032-ed7e355d5364\"\u003e\u003cac:parameter ac:name=\"breakoutMode\"\u003ewide\u003c/ac:parameter\u003e\u003cac:parameter ac:name=\"breakoutWidth\"\u003e760\u003c/ac:parameter\u003e\u003cac:plain-text-body\u003e\u003c![CDATA[1. Connect to the primary DB as a superuser: `psql -h db-primary.internal -U admin -d postgres`\n2. Run: `SELECT count(*), state FROM pg_stat_activity GROUP BY state;`\n3. Expected: idle connections \u003c 150, active connections \u003c 50\n4. If idle connections exceed 150, restart application servers to release idle connections (Step 2).\n5. If active connections are high, identify the source (Step 3).]]\u003e\u003c/ac:plain-text-body\u003e\u003c/ac:structured-macro\u003e\u003ch2 local-id=\"86c5b659040a\"\u003e\u003cac:emoticon ac:name=\"blue-star\" ac:emoji-shortname=\":wrench:\" ac:emoji-id=\"1f527\" ac:local-id=\"bcac2c20f951\" ac:emoji-fallback=\"🔧\" /\u003e Step 2 \u0026mdash; Release Idle Connections (Immediate Mitigation)\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cac:structured-macro ac:name=\"code\" ac:schema-version=\"1\" ac:local-id=\"d3095110075e\" ac:macro-id=\"afec525a-25a5-4da5-ac7a-aff267a61dc6\"\u003e\u003cac:parameter ac:name=\"breakoutMode\"\u003ewide\u003c/ac:parameter\u003e\u003cac:parameter ac:name=\"breakoutWidth\"\u003e760\u003c/ac:parameter\u003e\u003cac:plain-text-body\u003e\u003c![CDATA[Restarting application servers releases idle database connections without requiring database downtime.\n\n1. Identify application servers: `api-server-01`, `api-server-02`, `api-server-03`\n2. Restart one at a time, verifying health before proceeding to the next:\n   - `sudo systemctl restart api-server`\n   - Wait 60 seconds\n   - Check: `curl https://api-server-01.internal/health`\n3. After each restart, re-check connection count using the query in Step 1.\n4. Do not restart all app servers simultaneously â this causes a service outage.]]\u003e\u003c/ac:plain-text-body\u003e\u003c/ac:structured-macro\u003e\u003ch2 local-id=\"23da8f1929c6\"\u003e\u003cac:emoticon ac:name=\"bulb\" ac:emoji-shortname=\":bulb:\" ac:emoji-id=\"1f4a1\" ac:local-id=\"52a8a65c97ea\" ac:emoji-fallback=\"💡\" /\u003e Step 3 \u0026mdash; Identify Connection Sources\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cac:structured-macro ac:name=\"code\" ac:schema-version=\"1\" ac:local-id=\"20e081a1b0c6\" ac:macro-id=\"36d9434e-c6c5-429f-9a00-f78133c2dcf3\"\u003e\u003cac:parameter ac:name=\"breakoutMode\"\u003ewide\u003c/ac:parameter\u003e\u003cac:parameter ac:name=\"breakoutWidth\"\u003e760\u003c/ac:parameter\u003e\u003cac:plain-text-body\u003e\u003c![CDATA[1. Find which applications hold the most connections:\n   `SELECT application_name, count(*) FROM pg_stat_activity GROUP BY application_name ORDER BY count DESC;`\n2. Find long-running queries holding connections:\n   `SELECT pid, now() - pg_stat_activity.query_start AS duration, query FROM pg_stat_activity WHERE state != \u0027idle\u0027 ORDER BY duration DESC LIMIT 10;`\n3. If a single application has an abnormally high count, check its connection pool configuration.]]\u003e\u003c/ac:plain-text-body\u003e\u003c/ac:structured-macro\u003e\u003ch2 local-id=\"3593ce828059\"\u003e\u003cac:emoticon ac:name=\"blue-star\" ac:emoji-shortname=\":mag_right:\" ac:emoji-id=\"1f50e\" ac:local-id=\"083898479dc6\" ac:emoji-fallback=\"🔎\" /\u003e Step 4 \u0026mdash; Check for Missing Indexes\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cac:structured-macro ac:name=\"code\" ac:schema-version=\"1\" ac:local-id=\"127783352b19\" ac:macro-id=\"4240b91d-14c5-47d5-a578-d9403bc1d98e\"\u003e\u003cac:parameter ac:name=\"breakoutMode\"\u003ewide\u003c/ac:parameter\u003e\u003cac:parameter ac:name=\"breakoutWidth\"\u003e760\u003c/ac:parameter\u003e\u003cac:plain-text-body\u003e\u003c![CDATA[Slow queries can cause connections to pile up waiting for query completion.\n\n1. Check for sequential scans on large tables:\n   `SELECT relname, seq_scan, idx_scan FROM pg_stat_user_tables ORDER BY seq_scan DESC LIMIT 10;`\n2. If the `requests` table shows high sequential scan count, check for the index:\n   `SELECT indexname FROM pg_indexes WHERE tablename = \u0027requests\u0027;`\n3. If `idx_requests_created_at` is missing, create it:\n   `CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY idx_requests_created_at ON requests(created_at);`\n4. This operation runs without locking the table. Monitor progress with:\n   `SELECT phase, blocks_done, blocks_total FROM pg_stat_progress_create_index;`]]\u003e\u003c/ac:plain-text-body\u003e\u003c/ac:structured-macro\u003e\u003ch2 local-id=\"a5e16c40e7c7\"\u003e\u003cac:emoticon ac:name=\"fire\" ac:emoji-shortname=\":fire:\" ac:emoji-id=\"1f525\" ac:local-id=\"7e8a0e69f8f2\" ac:emoji-fallback=\"🔥\" /\u003e Step 5 \u0026mdash; Emergency: Terminate Idle Connections\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cac:structured-macro ac:name=\"code\" ac:schema-version=\"1\" ac:local-id=\"8bc0066e5b9f\" ac:macro-id=\"43254f8d-da57-4b09-9b49-53f1e3e3f790\"\u003e\u003cac:parameter ac:name=\"breakoutMode\"\u003ewide\u003c/ac:parameter\u003e\u003cac:parameter ac:name=\"breakoutWidth\"\u003e760\u003c/ac:parameter\u003e\u003cac:plain-text-body\u003e\u003c![CDATA[If connection count is at max and Step 2 is not fast enough:\n\n1. Terminate idle connections older than 10 minutes:\n   `SELECT pg_terminate_backend(pid) FROM pg_stat_activity WHERE state = \u0027idle\u0027 AND query_start \u003c now() - interval \u002710 minutes\u0027;`\n2. This is a last resort. Prefer the graceful restart in Step 2.]]\u003e\u003c/ac:plain-text-body\u003e\u003c/ac:structured-macro\u003e\u003ch2 local-id=\"1b97e298456c\"\u003e\u003cac:emoticon ac:name=\"blue-star\" ac:emoji-shortname=\":telephone:\" ac:emoji-id=\"260e\" ac:local-id=\"88bfea1a8222\" ac:emoji-fallback=\"âï¸\" /\u003e Step 6 \u0026mdash; Escalation\u003c/h2\u003e\u003ctable data-table-width=\"760\" data-layout=\"default\" ac:local-id=\"2603247551c1\" data-table-display-mode=\"default\"\u003e\u003ctbody\u003e\u003ctr ac:local-id=\"d6c8e85ed459\"\u003e\u003cth ac:local-id=\"edbe0721e166\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"9c5dbe63a8ce\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eAction\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/th\u003e\u003cth ac:local-id=\"c13fb124faf8\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"17436879987d\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDetails\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/th\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr ac:local-id=\"ac0e847e9108\"\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"fdc3c523cf96\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"09b4064e7e74\"\u003ePage on-call DBA\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"f8172ff3731e\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"cb30cf6ffc70\"\u003ePage the on-call DBA via PagerDuty: escalation policy `DBA-ONCALL`\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr ac:local-id=\"74d3c09679a6\"\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"86106500ba66\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"0e83b381abe3\"\u003eNotify Slack\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"6459a18fcc24\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"d6b0ad015b86\"\u003eNotify `#incidents` Slack channel\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr ac:local-id=\"2d1e349171e3\"\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"dbe794fdb521\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"321ab80506a6\"\u003eConsider increasing max_connections\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"523abbf60934\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"7f9124411672\"\u003eConsider temporarily increasing `max_connections` in `postgresql.conf` (requires DB restart \u0026mdash; coordinate with DBA)\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003c/tbody\u003e\u003c/table\u003e\u003ch2 local-id=\"d7d74623c4b2\"\u003e\u003cac:emoticon ac:name=\"chart_with_upwards_trend\" ac:emoji-shortname=\":chart_with_upwards_trend:\" ac:emoji-id=\"1f4c8\" ac:local-id=\"75827191e654\" ac:emoji-fallback=\"📈\" /\u003e Monitoring\u003c/h2\u003e\u003ctable data-table-width=\"760\" data-layout=\"default\" ac:local-id=\"6ebbcc359e22\" data-table-display-mode=\"default\"\u003e\u003ctbody\u003e\u003ctr ac:local-id=\"a1dd9eed946c\"\u003e\u003cth ac:local-id=\"7e5a6f677c80\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"70571e7e76e1\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eItem\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/th\u003e\u003cth ac:local-id=\"d3ad1bad65df\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"c2eda1e729dd\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDetails\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/th\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr ac:local-id=\"3312922ce58f\"\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"384abec20d44\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"8df6738eef5b\"\u003eGrafana dashboard\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"4444b2ba22b5\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"a4e7ea184dfd\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://grafana.internal/dashboard/postgresql\"\u003ePostgreSQL Overview\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr ac:local-id=\"8ff17076702b\"\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"1a59de72f8bd\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"3e27786458e3\"\u003eAlert: connection count\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"631c4018e440\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"c2079baff7ab\"\u003eConnection count above 180 for 3 consecutive minutes triggers PagerDuty\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr ac:local-id=\"0f01a1693cb6\"\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"b45d5dc0ce77\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"ab5903461e71\"\u003eAlert: query duration\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd ac:local-id=\"d4cdcd85b113\" valign=\"top\"\u003e\u003cp local-id=\"036a5d283f40\"\u003eQuery duration above 10 seconds triggers warning in `#db-alerts`\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003c/tbody\u003e\u003c/table\u003e"
                              },
                  "4489217":  {
                                  "title":  "VPN Gateway Recovery Runbook",
                                  "storage":  "\u003cac:structured-macro ac:name=\"code\" ac:schema-version=\"1\" ac:local-id=\"9a2eab0f-5bd7-43be-8d3d-49d14a43ef2f\" ac:macro-id=\"de9bb983-e588-48d7-998a-21c91bb5a0ae\"\u003e\u003cac:parameter ac:name=\"language\"\u003emarkdown\u003c/ac:parameter\u003e\u003cac:parameter ac:name=\"breakoutMode\"\u003ewide\u003c/ac:parameter\u003e\u003cac:parameter ac:name=\"breakoutWidth\"\u003e760\u003c/ac:parameter\u003e\u003cac:parameter ac:name=\"wrap\"\u003etrue\u003c/ac:parameter\u003e\u003cac:plain-text-body\u003e\u003c![CDATA[### Overview\n\nThis runbook covers diagnosis and recovery of the corporate VPN gateway (`vpn.corp.internal`). The VPN gateway runs OpenVPN on UDP port 1194 and provides remote access for all employees working outside the office. Existing sessions are typically unaffected by gateway issues; new connection attempts fail.\n\n### Symptoms\n\n- Remote workers unable to establish new VPN connections\n- VPN client shows \"connection timed out\" after 60 seconds\n- Existing VPN sessions remain active\n- UDP port 1194 not responding: `nc -uvz vpn.corp.internal 1194` times out\n\n### Architecture\n\n- **Gateway host:** `vpn-gw-01.corp.internal` (primary), `vpn-gw-02.corp.internal` (standby)\n- **Protocol:** OpenVPN over UDP port 1194\n- **Firewall:** Palo Alto firewall, managed by network team\n- **Failover:** Manual â no automatic failover between primary and standby\n\n### Step 1 â Check Gateway Reachability\n\n1. Ping the gateway: `ping vpn.corp.internal`\n2. Check UDP port: `nc -uvz vpn.corp.internal 1194`\n   - If this times out, the issue is likely a firewall rule (Step 2)\n   - If ping succeeds but UDP fails, the OpenVPN process may be down (Step 3)\n3. Check HTTPS management interface: `https://vpn-gw-01.corp.internal:943/admin`\n\n### Step 2 â Check Firewall Rules\n\nFirewall rule changes are the most common cause of VPN connectivity failures for new connections.\n\n1. Log in to the Palo Alto firewall admin console: `https://firewall.corp.internal`\n2. Navigate to: **Policies â Security â Inbound**\n3. Look for rules affecting `vpn-gw-01.corp.internal` on UDP port 1194\n4. Check the change log: **Monitor â Logs â Config** â filter by last 2 hours\n5. If a recent rule change is found that blocks UDP 1194, revert it:\n   - Right-click the rule â **Revert to previous version**\n   - Click **Commit** to apply\n6. Verify: re-run `nc -uvz vpn.corp.internal 1194` â should respond within 5 seconds\n7. Document the reverted rule in the change management system\n\n### Step 3 â Check OpenVPN Process\n\nIf the firewall is not the issue, check the OpenVPN service on the gateway host.\n\n1. SSH to the gateway: `ssh admin@vpn-gw-01.corp.internal`\n2. Check service status: `sudo systemctl status openvpn@server`\n3. If the service is stopped, start it: `sudo systemctl start openvpn@server`\n4. Check logs for errors: `sudo journalctl -u openvpn@server --since \"1 hour ago\"`\n5. Common errors:\n   - `TLS Error: TLS handshake failed` â certificate issue, contact network team\n   - `Cannot open TUN/TAP dev /dev/net/tun` â kernel module not loaded: `sudo modprobe tun`\n   - `Address already in use` â another process on port 1194: `sudo lsof -i :1194`\n\n### Step 4 â Failover to Standby Gateway\n\nIf the primary gateway cannot be recovered within 15 minutes:\n\n1. Update DNS: change `vpn.corp.internal` to point to `vpn-gw-02.corp.internal`\n   - TTL is 60 seconds â new connections will use the standby within 1 minute\n2. Notify users to reconnect their VPN clients\n3. Open a ticket with the network team to repair the primary gateway\n4. Do not failover and repair the primary simultaneously\n\n### Step 5 â Escalation\n\nIf VPN connectivity is not restored within 20 minutes:\n\n- Page the on-call network engineer via PagerDuty: escalation policy `NETWORK-ONCALL`\n- Notify `#incidents` Slack channel with number of affected users\n- If \u003e50% of remote workforce is affected, declare a P1 incident\n\n### Monitoring\n\n- VPN connection count dashboard: [VPN Overview](https://grafana.internal/dashboard/vpn)\n- Alert: new connection success rate below 90% for 5 minutes triggers PagerDuty\n- Alert: UDP port 1194 unresponsive for 2 minutes triggers immediate page\n\n### Known Issues\n\n- **Certificate renewal**: OpenVPN server certificates expire annually. Renewal requires a brief service restart (\u003c 30 seconds). Schedule during low-usage hours.\n- **UDP fragmentation**: Some corporate hotel/conference networks block UDP. In these cases, users should switch to TCP mode in their VPN client settings]]\u003e\u003c/ac:plain-text-body\u003e\u003c/ac:structured-macro\u003e"
                              }
              }
}